            "level": {
                "value": 3
            },
            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>A bogey typically hunts a single creature at a time, usually a small child or elderly person, methodically stalking and tormenting their prey. Often hiding under a bed, amid a dark attic space, or in a closet left slightly ajar, a bogey delights in the slow, methodical cultivation of fear in their victims until the time comes to reap their soul.</p><hr /><p>Bogeymen are stealers of innocence and devourers of souls. Few targets who survive an encounter with them remain untouched by repeated nightmares, feelings of paranoia, and newly realized phobias. Different names are given to bogeymen according to their varying sizes and degrees of power, which typically grow stronger and stronger as the monsters consume more and more souls.</p>\n<p>Many bogeymen look like the mortal folk that they prey on, allowing them to often hide in plain sight.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Pathfinder Feybound"
            }
